single-file-selection fix; replays merged PR #98, reverted in f4e40cef)
Task: Delete test:quick per Peter's decision 2026-08-02
Agent: Claude (main session)
Unit: this chore (single commit)

## What

- Removes the root `test:quick` script from package.json.
- ALSO removes duplicate `test:performance` / `test:performance:isolated`
  keys that the revert (f4e40cef) introduced — see below.
- Re-adds dated removal notes to the two historical docs that documented
  test:quick; the revert had stripped them.

## Why deletion (Peter's call, offered delete vs. lane-config fix)

- Same footgun as the `npm test` one fixed in #97: trailing array-typed
  `--testPathIgnorePatterns` means `npm run test:quick -- <file>` ADDS the
  file as an ignore pattern instead of selecting it.
- Unused: no CI workflow, hook, or steering doc references it — only two
  historical spec docs and the shipped 14.0.0 release notes.
- Rationale void: since the 2026-07-03 lane rework (`29bba7de`),
  `test:quick` was just `npm test` minus the integration suites on a
  ~1-minute lane; skipping integration coverage invites false-green
  validation.

## Revert-collateral defect fixed here (NOT in original #98 scope)

f4e40cef reverted #98 against a package.json since changed by #97, and the
context mismatch duplicated two script keys:

    "test:performance"          (lines 114 and 116)
    "test:performance:isolated" (lines 115 and 117)

JSON.parse accepts duplicates silently (last-wins) and both copies were
identical, so behavior was unaffected — but the manifest was malformed.
The duplicates sit on the exact lines this chore edits, so they are removed
here rather than left on main. Resulting package.json blob is byte-identical
to the pre-revert state (4f7b096c).

## Validation

- `npm test`: 367/367 suites, 8891/8891 tests green.
- package.json parses; zero duplicate script keys (40 scripts total);
  `test:performance` and `test:performance:isolated` still resolve.
- Repo-wide grep: no remaining operational `test:quick` reference.

